+    The stops are px, not percentages, so the ramp is independent of the
+    element's height and every consumer keeps working untouched — including the
+    `background-size`-less toolbar rules and JournalPublisher's multi-layer
+    shorthand (src/SynApps/JournalPublisher.app/…/styles.css:198,443), which
+    pass these through as a `background-image` value. A gradient has no
+    intrinsic size, so it fills its whole positioning area; anchoring the ramp
+    to one edge in px and leaving the remainder transparent reproduces the
+    27px band exactly and makes the consumers' `repeat-x` a harmless no-op.
+
+    Stop maths: a device row y samples the gradient at its centre y+0.5, so
+    a(p) = 171/255 · (26.5 − p)/26 → a(0) = 0.6835, reaching zero at 26.5px.
